Q: Unsure how to go about replicating React Component lifecycle methods through useEffect() where componentDidMount calls a function within a function
A: <p>I would like to suggest the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>If you are using functional components, work with the 'useState' hook to manage the state. You can later reference the destructured variables and methods freely as long as they are within the scope of the component, without using 'this'.</li>
</ul>
<pre><code>const [scripts, setScripts] = useState();

// Inside render:
&lt;h1&gt; {scripts.length} &lt;/h1&gt;
// ...
&lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setScripts([])}&gt; Erase Scripts &lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Same concept with methods you create:</li>
</ul>
<pre><code>const handleScriptButtonClick = () =&gt; {};

// Inside render:
&lt;button onClick={handleScriptButtonClick}&gt; Script &lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li><p>Try to avoid using indices as keys in arrays if you can. Ideally find some other unique identifier.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Try to avoid using the state to store a big list of elements or components. It's preferable to store the data associated with the buttons you want to create and then build them inside the render method. Something like this:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<pre><code>render() {
// ...
&lt;section&gt;
      { scripts.map((script, i) =&gt; 
        &lt;button key={script.id} onClick={() =&gt; handleScriptButtonClick(script)}&gt;
          Script {i}
        &lt;/button&gt;
      )}
 &lt;/section&gt;
}
</code></pre>

Q: set method for useState Hook doesn't re-render used Hooks
A: <p>The <code>useEffect</code> and <code>useLayoutEffect</code> hooks get a second parameter of dependent state which will be used to evaluate if the hook has to rerun. </p>

<p><code>useEffect(callback, dependencies)</code></p>

<p><code>useLayoutEffect(callback, dependencies)</code></p>

<p>See: <a href="https://reactjs.org/docs/hooks-reference.html#uselayouteffect" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://reactjs.org/docs/hooks-reference.html#uselayouteffect</a></p>

<p>So in your example make sure that <code>favorit</code> is included in the list of dependencies of the <code>useLayoutEffect</code>:</p>

<pre><code>React.useLayoutEffect(() =&gt; {
    alert('re-render with: ' + favorit);
    navigation.setOptions({
        headerRight: () =&gt; &lt;HeaderRight /&gt;,
    });
}, [navigation, favorit]);
</code></pre>

