Q: How do I reference Entity Framework 6 from a .NET core class library in RC2?
A: <p>Entity Framework 6.1.3 does not support .NET Core. This was part of the motivation for creating Entity Framework Core. EF 6 has deep ties to APIs in .NET Framework that may not be ported to exist in .NET Core.</p>

<p>You can still use EF6 with "project.json" projects but you need to target .NET Framework instead of .NET Core.</p>

<pre><code>{
    "dependencies": {
        "EntityFramework": "6.1.3"
    },
    "frameworks": {
        "net461": { }
    }
}
</code></pre>
